Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

SWP-1 is built from source against the following crates. Each is listed here
because the threat model's [§10, "Parser exploitation"](docs/THREAT-MODEL.md#10-parser-exploitation)
treats the dependency list as part of the trusted surface: the binary you run
links exactly these, and `swp` opens no socket in any code path. The
authoritative versions are in `Cargo.lock`.

  sha2, hmac            Apache-2.0 OR MIT        RustCrypto hashes and MAC
  ed25519-dalek         BSD-3-Clause             dalek signatures
  curve25519-dalek      BSD-3-Clause             transitive, via ed25519-dalek
  getrandom             Apache-2.0 OR MIT        operating system randomness
  subtle                BSD-3-Clause             constant-time primitives
  zeroize               Apache-2.0 OR MIT        clearing secret material
  serde, serde_json     Apache-2.0 OR MIT        data model and canonical JSON
  thiserror             Apache-2.0 OR MIT        error types
  walkdir               MIT OR Unlicense         directory traversal
  zip                   MIT                      container reading (deflate only)
  tar                   Apache-2.0 OR MIT        container reading
  flate2                Apache-2.0 OR MIT        inflation (rust backend only)
  time                  Apache-2.0 OR MIT        RFC 3339 timestamps
  unicode-normalization Apache-2.0 OR MIT        text preprocessing
  base64                Apache-2.0 OR MIT        encoding
  toml                  Apache-2.0 OR MIT        configuration files
  tree-sitter           MIT                      incremental parsing runtime
  tree-sitter-javascript    MIT                  grammar
  tree-sitter-typescript    MIT                  grammar
  tree-sitter-python        MIT                  grammar

The license identifiers above are read from each component's own manifest rather
than from memory, and the set is exactly the `[workspace.dependencies]` table in
`Cargo.toml` — every line of the product's third-party surface, with
`curve25519-dalek` named because it is the one transitive dependency that carries
a primitive.

Full license texts are distributed with the corresponding source. None of these
components is modified, forked, or relicensed by this project, and none of them
performs any network I/O.

